@openwaters/maritime-zones

The code in this package is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). The data files in
dist/ are derived from the Marine Regions Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase,
published by the Flanders Marine Institute (VLIZ) under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Changes: polygons are rounded to 1e-5 degrees and subdivided into small
pieces (zones.fgb); zone and coastline rings are split into short lines
(boundaries.fgb, land.fgb); attributes are renamed and reduced.

Cite each layer as:

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Internal
Waters, version 4. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/.
https://doi.org/10.14284/631

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase:
Archipelagic Waters, version 4. Available online at
https://www.marineregions.org/. https://doi.org/10.14284/629

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Territorial
Seas (12NM), version 4. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/.
https://doi.org/10.14284/633

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Contiguous
Zones (24NM), version 4. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/.
https://doi.org/10.14284/630

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Maritime
Boundaries and Exclusive Economic Zones (200NM), version 12. Available online
at https://www.marineregions.org/. https://doi.org/10.14284/632

Flanders Marine Institute (2024). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: High Seas,
version 2. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/.
https://doi.org/10.14284/696

Coastline (land.fgb): Marine Regions land_v9, the coastline used for
Maritime Boundaries v9. Its licence is being confirmed with Marine Regions;
do not publish until it is.
